{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261117T054305Z-167264c1", "ts": "2026-11-17T05:46:19Z", "actor": {"worktree": "ldm", "plugin": "3.8.1", "branch": "fix/nats-lame-duck-feed-loss"}, "body": {"base_commit": "821bbc669dbc99365ff063478eea568ed86f53b2", "base_tree": "61a93d82aeaa916b823012f9844f14f34378fe82", "head_tree": "1acb3e148b5ce46032ae8227ee5d4737fd85ca42", "head_commit": "b669b91cb425778884ef0063a445217a69f68782", "dispatch_commit": "b669b91cb425778884ef0063a445217a69f68782", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "rule-2 cumulative: branch is 2 commits ahead of origin/develop, working tree clean, no fresh cumulative-mode record for current HEAD, and no composed review coverage spans the branch", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "docs/nats-credential-renewal.md", "packages/nats/src/threetears/nats/client.py", "packages/nats/tests/unit/test_connection_handover.py", "packages/nats/tests/unit/test_reconnect_backoff.py"], "files_changed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "docs/nats-credential-renewal.md", "packages/nats/src/threetears/nats/client.py", "packages/nats/tests/unit/test_connection_handover.py", "packages/nats/tests/unit/test_reconnect_backoff.py"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No test evidence for the reviewed tree", "recommendation": "instance: prawduct-hook test-status reports 'stale: no .test-evidence.json on disk' in this worktree, so nothing shows the nats unit suite (test_connection_handover.py, test_reconnect_backoff.py) or the lame-duck integration test passed on b669b91cb. Run the suite and record evidence before the PR.", "files": ["packages/nats/tests/unit/test_connection_handover.py", "packages/nats/tests/unit/test_reconnect_backoff.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "The never-reconnect fix is tested only against a fake that assumes the mechanism it rests on", "recommendation": "instance: _hand_over sets previous.options['allow_reconnect'] = False after connect and relies on nats-py re-reading that dict entry in _process_op_err when the server drops the connection. test_a_replaced_connection_closes_when_its_server_drops_it_rather_than_reconnecting asserts only that the flag was written on a _Conn fake whose options dict was added to mirror that assumption; no test drops a real nats-py connection and observes that it closes without reconnecting or replaying SUBs. nats-py already copies other connect options into private fields (reconnect_to_server_handler -> _reconnect_to_server_handler), and the nats-py cap procedure in _nats_py_internals.py does not list this dependency, so a nats-py release that does the same here reverts the fix silently. Add a wire_server test (as test_nats_py_internals.py does) that connects a real Client with allow_reconnect True, sets the option False, has the server close the socket, and asserts is_closed and no reconnect; name the dependency where the cap procedure will see it.", "files": ["packages/nats/src/threetears/nats/client.py", "packages/nats/tests/unit/test_connection_handover.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "Least-tried selection slows reconnect backoff growth by the pool size, unrecorded", "recommendation": "instance: the delay is still keyed on the selected server's reconnects, but the selected server is now the least-tried one, so with N servers the exponent rises about once per N failed attempts instead of once per attempt (base 1, cap 30, 3 servers: ceilings 1,1,1,2,2,2,4,4,4... where they were 1,2,4,8,16,30). In a full-cluster outage (the Hub restart resilience-task-06 exists for) each client retries roughly N times as often before reaching the cap, and a server whose count was reset when it last connected, or one learned from INFO connect_urls, drops the delay back to base. The docstring still says 'the per-attempt count drives the backoff'. Either key the delay on a count that rises every attempt (for example the max reconnects across the snapshot) while still choosing the least-tried server, or record that the slower growth is accepted and why; add a test that the ceiling keeps rising across a dead pool.", "files": ["packages/nats/src/threetears/nats/client.py", "packages/nats/tests/unit/test_reconnect_backoff.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "allow_reconnect=False does not stop a reconnect already under way", "recommendation": "instance: nats-py's _attempt_reconnect loop never re-reads allow_reconnect, so a handover that promotes while the old connection is already RECONNECTING (a requested renewal during a partial outage; renew_connection checks only is_closed) leaves it reconnecting, and on success it replays the old halves' SUBs, which stay registered until the retirement drain. Narrow window; consider refusing or closing a leaving connection that is not connected at promotion.", "files": ["packages/nats/src/threetears/nats/client.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Renewal procedure step 5 still promises the old connection serves replies until retirement", "recommendation": "instance: docs/nats-credential-renewal.md step 5 says that until retirement 'a reply to a request sent on it still arrives there'. With this change a replaced connection its server drops closes instead of reconnecting, so requests still waiting on it end at the drop. Make the claim relational (until retirement or until its server drops it); the lame-duck section already says the connection is never reconnected.", "files": ["docs/nats-credential-renewal.md"], "fid": "R-5"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 3, "note": 2}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound",